---
/** How to use a downloaded skill. Shared by the skills hub and every skill page. */
interface Props {
	/** Skill folder name, when shown on a skill page. */
	slug?: string;
}
const { slug = 'skill-name' } = Astro.props;
---

<section aria-labelledby="install" class="prose">
	<h2 id="install">How to install a skill</h2>
	<p>
		A skill is a folder with a <code>SKILL.md</code> file: YAML frontmatter with a <code>name</code> and a
		<code>description</code>, then plain Markdown instructions. An assistant reads the description to decide when the skill
		applies and loads the rest only then. The format is the open
		<a href="https://agentskills.io/specification" rel="noopener">Agent Skills specification</a>.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Claude Code:</strong> unzip the download so the folder lands in <code>~/.claude/skills/{slug}/</code> for all
			projects, or <code>.claude/skills/{slug}/</code> inside one project. Start a new session.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Claude app (web and desktop):</strong> upload the zip in the Skills section of your settings. Availability depends
			on your plan, and the menu names change, so check Anthropic's current help pages.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Other assistants that support Agent Skills:</strong> copy the folder into the skills directory that assistant
			documents.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Any other LLM:</strong> open <code>SKILL.md</code> and paste its contents into the system prompt, custom
			instructions or project instructions. You lose automatic loading, but the guidance works the same.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Skills that work with your org need a connection: a Salesforce MCP server added to your assistant, or the
		<a href="/docs/sf-cli/salesforce-cli-reference-guide/">Salesforce CLI</a> logged in to an org. Start with a sandbox or
		scratch org, and give the connection the least access that does the job.
	</p>
</section>
